{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"The unitary fee is paid by the fund to the adviser. The adviser typically retains the management-fee revenue, while the brand sponsor’s separate contract reimburses or pays specified ordinary operating expenses for the fee remainder; the adviser and sponsor allocate that economics under their contract. There is no standard percentage split—terms vary by fund and agreement.\n\nThe sponsor’s assumption does **not** eliminate the adviser’s continuing obligation to the fund: the adviser remains responsible for ensuring the fund’s covered expenses are paid as required by the advisory agreement and prospectus, even if it must cover costs the sponsor fails to pay under their separate arrangement."}}
